From 03903bb58defaabba0d99177d4021c9dcd9c244c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: FCA11 feel fix round - wobble damping, gentle-ask
 gain, low-speed restore, lead-loss hold (0051)

Drive-feedback 15b-15f (130 min on 0049, dev e874835ad0). Braking is better, but:
(1) gentle asks over-deliver ~2x; (2) 0049 raised the wire dip-and-recover count (the pre-0049
law replayed on THESE drives gives 29; the "24" quoted in the first round is the older
158/159/15a cohort); (3) a radar lead drop-out mid-brake (15c seg 45, 47 km/h) produced a
release-and-reapply. Python only, OLD-LAW feel path only (self.feel). No panda/safety change.

(a) WOBBLE. Root cause, isolated by open-loop replay of the real class over the drives:
the 0049 ANTICIPATION term. Its slope EMA (alpha 0.2 per sent frame) follows the
planner's +-0.05 m/s^2 ask ripple, so the anticipated ask flickers and the follow-down
target flips 1-3 LSB frame to frame. Fix: anticipation reads a slower EMA
(FCA11_FEEL_SLOPE_ALPHA_0051 = 0.10; the 0.2 EMA still drives the deepening bypass,
unchanged), plus a RE-RISE DEADBAND: after the level came down from the episode peak, a
gentle not-fast-deepening ask must call for >= FCA11_FEEL_RERISE_LSB (2) more before the
level climbs again. Onsets, harder asks and fast-building asks are untouched.

(b) GENTLE GAIN. Steady per-level delivered on the drives fits an affine plant
(brake-only = 0.57 + 8.06 * L/100 m/s^2, ~1.0 m/s^2 bite at L 4-7), so below ~1 m/s^2
no level can deliver the ask; the 5/6/7 clean steady samples are thin. Not a per-level
table: a single PARTIAL gain on the feel target, FCA11_FEEL_GENTLE_GAIN = 0.70 =
sqrt(1/2.03) (half the measured (-1.0,-0.7] over-delivery in log terms), for asks
at/above -0.8, fading to 1.0 at the HARD bypass (-1.2). A HARD ask stays byte-identical.

(b2) LOW-SPEED RESTORE. The stop/hold band (<= 3 km/h or standstill) runs the DEPLOYED
law, not the feel law, so a level left ~2-3 LSB low by (b) RE-STEPPED at band entry: an
independent adversarial review measured a +4 LSB step on 18 of the 25 scored stops, in the
last ~0.6 s before standstill (0049: 0/25; caused by (b) alone), i.e. the last metre went
firm and jerky, the opposite of this round's intent. Fix: the gain is faded back to 1.0 as
the car slows (FCA11_FEEL_GAIN_FADE_KPH 8.0 -> FCA11_FEEL_GAIN_FULL_KPH 5.0, a continuous
curve, no latch - a latch over it is provably inert), so the level ARRIVES at the deployed
request and the band cannot step it. The strength correction stays where it was measured
(at speed; the delivered/ask table is taken > 15 km/h and is unchanged). Replay: +4 at band
entry 18/25 -> 0/25 scored stops; the band-entry profile is 0049's exactly (rise med 1,
max 4, +4 in 4 of 36 entries); predicted delivered over the last 0.6 s before standstill
rises 0.29 -> 0.03 m/s^2 median and the last-second peak jerk 3.36 -> 1.22 m/s^3 (0049:
0.02 / 1.20).

(c) LEAD-LOSS HOLD. On a radarState.leadOne present -> absent edge inside an open
moving feel episode, the last SENT level becomes a floor: held while the lead stays
absent (<= 1.0 s) and 0.6 s more, then tapered to 0 over 1.0 s. Bounded by the level
already on the wire AND the PRE-0049 deployed request for the current ask (never more than
the pre-0049 law would command); no anticipation while active; every `ok` veto and the
-0.30 + min-on exit rule are unchanged. 15c seg 45 replay: level floor 4 -> 8.

The lead fields are now a CONTROL INPUT for (c), not the log-only reads 0045 documented;
the module comment says so (the matching "Log-only reads" line in carcontroller.py is
stale and is flagged for the next fork commit - this patch does not touch that file).

Kill switch FCA11_FEEL_FIX_0051 = False: replay byte-identical to the 0050 chain on all
four drives, and the whole hyundai suite passes with it OFF (the first round failed 1 test
there; that test now follows the instance). Tests: new test_fca11_feel_fix.py (35) - the
low-speed restore curve/endpoints and the band-entry step, plus the bounds the review found
unpinned: the lead-loss floor never above the level on the wire, the literal hold/taper/
max-absent times, the deadband/gain boundaries; three 0049/0041 tests that pinned "steady
level unchanged" now pin the gentle-gain level (<= deployed, == deployed for a HARD ask).

Replay (open loop, the real class over the recorded 15b/c/e/f inputs): wire dips 109 -> 28
(was 27 without (b2): one LSB of ask ripple re-exposed at 6-8 km/h, and 13 dips at <= 3 km/h
removed); onsets/release counts and episode open/close frames unchanged (on/off differs 0 of
29,524 frames); predicted delivered/ask 2.14 -> 1.72 (-0.7,-0.5] and 1.98 -> 1.66
(-1.0,-0.7]; lead-loss drop-and-reapply 5 -> 2 of 19 in-brake edges; last-second predicted
delivered mean 1.65 -> 1.64 (the restore hands the last metre back to the 0049 level).
0 send slots above the pre-0049 law on any drive.

Closed loop (wsH harness, 124 windows of 157/158/159/15a): the FCA wire dip-and-recover
count and the delivered-cycle count are in the workspace report. CAVEAT: the harness never
sets CS.fca11_lead_one, so the (c) hold never ran in sim - the closed-loop evidence covers
(a) + (b) + (b2) only, and it has no 15x windows (the plant's 4-8 LSB band is provisional).
Treat the next drive as the measurement drive.
